spec:
  grid: 10-30 square, background black(0)
  plus_shapes:
    count: 2-5
    shape: green(3) four-arm cross with 1-cell arms around a center pixel
    center_color: each distinct; exactly 0-1 may equal bg (acts as gap emitter)
    placement: all centers on unique rows and unique columns; no two plus shapes share cells (min Chebyshev distance between centers >= 3); arms may touch grid edge (min arm-to-edge distance >= 0)
    only_foreground: every non-bg pixel in input belongs to exactly one plus shape
  rays:
    rule: from each plus, emit 4 axis-aligned rays (L/R/U/D) in center color starting 2 cells from center; ray paints bg cells until hitting a foreground pixel or grid edge
    ordering: horizontal rays painted first, then vertical rays overwrite at crossings
    gap_effect: a bg-centered plus emits bg-colored vertical rays that erase horizontal colored rays at crossing points, creating visible gaps
    interaction: at least some rays should extend >= 2 cells [observed]; some rays get blocked by other pluses' foreground in 4/5 examples [observed]
generation_strategy:
  approach: direct placement with separation constraints
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N in [10..30] and num_plus in [2..5].
    2. Choose num_plus distinct colors from non-green palette; pick 0 or 1 to be bg(0), rest are marker colors.
    3. Place plus centers one at a time on the grid ensuring unique rows, unique columns, Chebyshev distance >= 3 to all prior centers, and arms stay within bounds (center row/col in [1..N-2]).
    4. Assign each chosen color to a center. Set all arm cells to green(3), center cell to its color.
    5. Verify every non-bg cell is part of a plus (guaranteed by construction since nothing else is placed).
```
